# apps/console — environment overrides.
#
# `config.yaml` is now the primary server configuration document (YAML-first, matching
# lightbridge-authz's config/default.yaml shape — see README.md and src/server/config-loader.ts).
# This file is no longer the config surface itself: it only supplies values for the `{env:VAR}`
# placeholders config.yaml actually references — secrets, plus anything else genuinely
# machine-local. Everything else (issuer URL, backend URLs, audiences, ...) lives as a literal in
# config.yaml; to change one of those for a real deployment, ship a different config.yaml and point
# CONSOLE_CONFIG at it, rather than adding an env var here.

# ── Session encryption ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cookie-session JWE key material (A256GCM via an HKDF of this value). At least 32 characters.
# Deploy-time secret: rotating it invalidates every live session. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Keycloak / OIDC ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only for a confidential client. The dev realm's `self-service` client is public + PKCE, so leave
# this unset there; setting it switches the client to `client_secret_post` authentication.
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Config document path ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides which YAML file config.yaml's loader reads, resolved against the app's own working
# directory (`pnpm --filter console dev|start` and `turbo run build:web` both run with cwd =
# apps/console). Defaults to ./config.yaml — a real deployment that needs different literals
# (issuer, backend URLs, ...) points this at its own file instead of editing env vars per field.
#
# No lightbridge-authz checkout locally? `docker compose up -d wiremock` (repo root compose.yml,
# port 18888) stubs the ops every console screen calls — see wiremock/mappings/ and the README's
# "Dev without a backend: wiremock" section. config.wiremock.yaml is a ready-made alternate
# document (backendUrl/apiBasePath/budgetUrl swapped to point at it); point CONSOLE_CONFIG there:
# CONSOLE_CONFIG=./config.wiremock.yaml

# ── Report export: the typst-render sidecar (converse-frontends#453) ──────────────────────────
# Where `GET /api/reports/page` POSTs {template, data, assets} to have a PDF compiled
# (apps/typst-render). Read through config.yaml's `reports.typstRenderUrl: '{env:TYPST_RENDER_URL}'`.
# Locally: `pnpm turbo run build:web --filter=typst-render && docker compose up typst-render`.
#
# Leave it UNSET and nothing breaks — `format=csv` and `format=html` still work, and `format=pdf`
# answers a 502 saying the renderer is not configured rather than producing a chartless PDF.
# TYPST_RENDER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# ── Report template overrides ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Directory the console looks in for per-route template overrides, as
# `<CONSOLE_TEMPLATES_DIR>/<route>/report.typ`. Lookup is per FILE: a route with no override file
# falls back to the template shipped in `apps/console/templates/`, so pointing this at an empty
# (or non-existent) directory overrides nothing. The Helm chart always sets it to
# /config/console/templates; a dev checkout normally leaves it unset.
# CONSOLE_TEMPLATES_DIR=/config/console/templates
